[node name="Contenido" type="Label" parent="InfQua/ScrollContainer/VBoxContainer" unique_id=1557879172]
layout_mode = 2
theme_override_font_sizes/font_size = 30
text = "Game Rules

The game is divided into three main phases: placement, 
movement, and capture and victory

Phase 1: Setup and Placement

1. Starting Pieces: Each player starts with 5 pieces, for a total of 10 
pieces on the board.

2. Turn-Based Placement: Players take turns placing one piece at a 
time on empty points on the board.

3. No ¡QUA! During Placement: Players are not allowed to align 3 
pieces before all 10 pieces have been placed on the board. If a 
player does so during this phase, that line is permanently
 invalidated, and neither player can score a ¡QUA! on that line 
for the rest of the game.

Phase 2: Movement

4. One Move Per Turn: Once all 10 pieces have been placed, 
players take turns moving one piece per turn.

5. Adjacent Movement: Pieces can only move one point at a
 time to a connected, empty vertex. Jumping over other pieces or 
skipping points is not allowed.

Phase 3: Capture and Victory

6. ¡QUA! Reward: When a player aligns 3 of their own pieces 
along a valid line (achieving a ¡QUA!), they earn the right to 
remove one opponent's piece of their choice. Only one piece can 
be removed for each ¡QUA! achieved.

7. One-Time Lines: A ¡QUA! can only be scored once on the 
same three-point line. If the same line is formed again, it has no 
effect.

8. Victory Condition: A player who is left with only 2 pieces on 
the board immediately loses the game, as they can no longer 
form a new ¡QUA!."

